<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/testing/mount',
        '/hooks/on-start',
        '/hooks/on-stop',
        '/hooks/on-principal',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/dogfood/examples/crm/src/reports/lib/PipelineSummary.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the summary answers in process as it does on the wire'"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/app.test.ts',
            from: ["test('an App held by await using stops when its block ends"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Ask a handler for its answer in a test, with no port">
        <p><code>app.fetch</code> takes a <code>Request</code> through everything a served one
            goes through: the middleware, the argument checks and the status a refusal carries.
            Run <code>bun test</code> from the app's own directory.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { expect, test } from 'bun:test'
            import { createApp } from '@abide/abide/server'

            test('the summary answers as it does on the wire', async () => {
                await using app = await createApp()
                const answer = await app.fetch(
                    new Request('http://crm.invalid/reports/getSummary'),
                )
                expect(await answer.json()).toEqual({ open: 3, pipeline: 15500 })
            })
        `} />
        <p>Hold the app with <code>await using</code>. An app nobody stops leaves open what
            <code>onStart</code> opened, and the suite hangs with no report.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Call a handler signed in as a team member">
        <p><code>app.run</code> runs a function in one request's scope, signed in with the
            <code>principal</code> claims you give it. <code>app.fetch</code> takes the same
            option.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { createApp } from '@abide/abide/server'
            import getCommission from '../getCommission.handler.ts'

            await using app = await createApp()
            const commission = await app.run(async () => await getCommission(), {
                principal: { id: 'theo' },
            })
            expect(commission.amount).toBe('$6,200')
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Serve the app from a host of your own">
        <p><code>createApp</code> binds no socket. <code>app.listen</code> binds one when a host
            or a test needs a real port.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { createApp } from '@abide/abide/server'

            const app = await createApp()
            await app.listen({ port: 8080 })
            process.on('SIGTERM', () => app.stop())
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
